<title>AFGHANISTAN: GOVERNMENT LIST.</title>
<headline>GOVERNMENT LIST.</headline>
<text>
<p>AFGHANISTAN GOVERNMENT LIST (960927)</p>
<p>  ***********************************************************</p>
<p>  * 27 Sept 96 - Afghanistan's Taleban Islamic movement     *</p>
<p>  *		  announced an interim ruling council for the*</p>
<p>  *		  country to replace the collapsed government*</p>
<p>  *		  of President Burhanuddin Rabbani.	    *</p>
<p>  *		  Mullah Mohammad Rabbani is to head the     *</p>
<p>  *		  six-man council. The five other council    *</p>
<p>  *		  members are: Mullah Mohammad Hassan, Mullah*</p>
<p>  *		  Abdul Razzaq, Maulvi Shamsuddin, Mullah    *</p>
<p>  *		  Mohammad Ghaus and Mullah Mohammad Fazil.  *</p>
<p>  ***********************************************************</p>
<p> President..........................Prof Burhanuddin RABBANI**</p>
<p>    (Elected 30 Dec 92)			   (**SEE NOTE ABOVE)</p>
<p>				- - - - - - -</p>
<p>COALITION CABINET (Named 3 Jul 96)</p>
<p>(See end of list for party affiliations)</p>
<p> Prime Minister............................Gulbuddin HEKMATYAR</p>
<p>(Sworn in 26 Jun 96)</p>
<p>				- - - - - - -</p>
<p>MINISTERS:</p>
<p> Commerce.......................Said Hussein Alami BALKHI (HE)</p>
<p> Defence...............................Wahidullah SABAWOON (H)</p>
<p> Education.............................Ahmad Shah AHMADZAI (I)</p>
<p> Finance............................Abdul Hadi ARGHANDIWAL (H)</p>
<p> Information &amp; Culture...................Qiyamuddin KASHAF (I)</p>
<p> Interior...........................Mohammad Younus QANUNI (J)</p>
<p> Labour &amp; Social Welfare.............Sayed Hossein ANVARI (HA)</p>
<p> Martyrs &amp; Disabled....................Maulvi Samiullah NAJABI</p>
<p> Planning........................Sayed Mohammad Ali JAVID (HA)</p>
<p>				- - - - - - -</p>
<p>PARTY AFFILIATIONS:</p>
<p>H - Hezb-i-Islami</p>
<p>J - Jamiat-i-Islami</p>
<p>I - Ittehad-i-Islami</p>
<p>HA - Harakat-i-Islami</p>
<p>HE - Hezb-i-Wahdat (Akbari group)</p>
<p>				- - - - - - -</p>
<p>President of the Afghanistan Bank</p>
<p>	(Central Bank)....................Ghulam Mohammad YAILAQ</p>
<p>				- - - - - - -</p>
<p>	 NOTE: Any comments/queries on the content of this</p>
<p>		 government list, please contact the Reuter</p>
<p>		 Editorial Reference Unit, London, on (171) 542</p>
<p>		 7968.</p>
<p>			  (End Government List)</p>
